course: dictionary
lesson: 108
title: Small changes and new beginnings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An adjustment is a small change that makes something work better, fit better or be more correct. «Dad made a small adjustment to my bike seat so it was the right height.» The seat was not broken. It just needed a little change.
explain: Adjustment can also mean getting used to something new. «Ravi needed a short period of adjustment before he felt at home in his new school.» The verb is adjust: you adjust a watch, a bike seat or a recipe.
explain: Scientists and engineers make adjustments all the time. «The scientists made a slight adjustment to the experiment and tried again.» The word slight tells you the change was tiny. Clues like small, slight and new help you find the meaning.
fact: An adjustment is a small change, not a big one.
fact: «Adjustment» can mean a change that makes something work better or fit better.
fact: «Adjustment» can also mean getting used to a new situation, such as a new school.
fact: «Adjust» is the verb: you adjust a watch, a bike seat or a recipe.
fact: Useful phrases: make an adjustment, a slight adjustment, a period of adjustment.
exercise: «Dad made a small adjustment to the bike seat.» What is an adjustment here? | A brand new bike | A bike that has been thrown away | A ride around the park | *A small change to make it fit better
exercise: «After the move, Mia needed a period of adjustment to her new town.» What does adjustment mean here? | A fast car journey | Buying new furniture | Leaving the town for good | *Getting used to a new situation
exercise: «The scientists made a slight adjustment to the experiment.» What does slight tell you about the change? | *It was tiny | It was enormous and dangerous | It was made by a robot | It took all year
test: «Ravi made an adjustment to his recipe by adding less sugar.» What did Ravi do? | Wrote a brand new cookbook | Ate the cake at once | Threw the recipe away | *Changed the recipe a little to make it better
test: Which phrase means a small change to make something work better? | play a game | *make an adjustment | make a mess | take a nap
exam: «After the watch lost time, Mr Lee made a slight adjustment to it, and now it keeps the right time.» What did Mr Lee do to the watch? | Put it in the bin | Bought a brand new watch | Hid it in a drawer | *Made a small change so it keeps the right time
